WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.680
Low-impact cloud services are generally associated with limited adverse effects from a

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.080
security incident.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.780
That does not mean the service is unimportant,

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:10.500
and it definitely does not mean security can be ignored.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.710
It means the expected harm from a loss of confidentiality, integrity,

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:17.920
or availability is lower than it would be for more sensitive or mission-critical systems.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.360
The baseline should still drive disciplined implementation and evidence.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:24.400
Low-risk SaaS concepts, including tailored low-impact paths,

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.330
are meant to recognize that some software services have limited sensitivity,

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:31.609
limited complexity, and a narrower security footprint.

00:00:31.609 --> 00:00:35.160
A focused path can make sense when the service is genuinely low impact and the operating

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.365
model is simple enough to support reduced assessment complexity.

00:00:38.365 --> 00:00:42.660
That is different from pretending a complicated or sensitive system is low impact to avoid

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:43.440
work.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.520
Even in lower-impact scenarios, common responsibilities remain.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.360
Access control should be understandable.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:52.060
Logging should support accountability and investigation at the level appropriate for the

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:52.680
service.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.164
Vulnerability management should be active.

00:00:55.164 --> 00:00:56.685
Configuration should be managed.

00:00:56.685 --> 00:00:58.480
Incident response should be defined.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:00.080
Continuous monitoring should not disappear;

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.500
it should be scaled to the system context and risk.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.200
Low impact still requires a real security program.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.640
For small SaaS providers entering the federal market,

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:10.615
the low-impact conversation can be a useful starting point.

00:01:10.615 --> 00:01:14.150
It encourages the team to define the boundary, identify what data is handled,

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:16.600
clarify customer and provider responsibilities,

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.405
and prove that the service is operated in a controlled way.

00:01:19.405 --> 00:01:22.270
The best lower-impact packages are not thin packages;

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:25.890
they are focused packages where scope, evidence, and risk are clearly aligned.
